  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nIssued 220 PM MST MON NOV 2 2026\nA pair of weak upper level troughs will move through on \nThursday and Friday, bringing a 10-30% chance of showers to \nnorthern areas. QPF totals are expected to stay under 0.10\" for \nboth events combined. Snow levels will range from 5500-7000 ft \nMSL, so some of the higher peaks will see a light dusting. \nTemperatures will be near normal with light winds. An upper \nlevel ridge will build in over the weekend, with temperatures \nwarming to 5-10 degrees above normal by Sunday. Another upper \nlevel trough will approach the Pacific Northwest early next \nweek, ushering in low chances of showers by Monday night. \nTemperatures will be similarly warmer than normal on Monday with\nbreezier conditions Sunday and Monday as the system approaches.",
